{
  "dom_id": "step-t2247",
  "name": "Isoperimetric Polygons",
  "problem": "Let's take a look at the polygons depicted below and find their perimeters.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14169002/assets/69ef06a71f13625ad4525a03966f4a4c62ae2b2136b085e97b8dc02a6a6963cc.png)\n\nFrom the picture, we conclude that polygons I, II and III all have a perimeter of $10$ while polygon IV has a perimeter of $8.$ \n\nPolygons that have the same perimeter are called **isoperimetric**. So I, II and III are isoperimetric polygons.",
